      "text": "To solve this problem, we first need to determine the perimeter of the triangle. The perimeter of a triangle is the sum of the lengths of its sides. Given the side lengths of the triangle are 6.1 cm, 8.2 cm, and 9.7 cm, we can calculate the perimeter as follows:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter of the triangle} = 6.1 + 8.2 + 9.7\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that the square has the same perimeter as the triangle. Since a square has four equal sides, if we denote the side length of the square as \\( s \\), then the perimeter of the square is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter of the square} = 4s\n\\]\n\nSince the perimeters are equal, we have:\n\n\\[\n4s = 6.1 + 8.2 + 9.7\n\\]\n\nWe can solve for \\( s \\) by dividing the sum of the side lengths of the triangle by 4:\n\n\\[\n4s = 24\n\\]\n\n\\[\ns = \\frac{24}{4} = 6\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the side length of the square, we can calculate its area. The area \\( A \\) of a square is given by:\n\n\\[\nA = s^2\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the value of \\( s \\):\n\n\\[\nA = 6^2 = 36\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36}\n\\]",
